WEBVTT

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.050
Sometimes I think about problems
that can't be solved by thinking.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.040
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.210
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.290
If I get stuck thinking about something
that has no solution,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.210
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site
Yakushima UNESCO World Heritage Site

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.670
then my brain starts feeling
like a washcloth that's being wrung out.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.290
I give up!

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.370
Hiroko Matsukata!

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.380
In order to totally reset herself...

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.920
is leaving on a journey!

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.210
Don't raise your voice.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.630
I don't need to make it a real vacation.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.960
Just a short trip to a place where I can truly relax.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.290
A place where I'm massaged by magic hands.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.960
Viva massages!

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.010
Shigoto dekiru otoko sore ga kanojo no konomi

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.300
Kiai irete tsutometa no daga

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.870
Isogashii wa tsuman nai wa

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.540
Ima no kaisha kanari level takai hou dashi

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.710
Oyaji garami no kone mo aru kara

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.880
Yameru wakya nai shi

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:50.290
Itsumo boku wa hitori kiri

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.500
Furo ni haitte neru dake

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.880
Nagameru koto sae dekinai

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.340
Kimi no kami o aruku sugata o

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.620
Nerukoto shika dekinai

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:18.920
Semete yume no naka de demo

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.920
Kimi ni aitai

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.910
Meticulous Man

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:30.840
Huh?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.500
Shirakawa-san isn't here today?

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.000
I'm very sorry about that.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.670
Ah, it's okay. What do I do now...?

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.880
Would you be all right with a different staff member?

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.540
Shirakawa-san hasn't taken a day off
since this work year started.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.750
That's why last month they decided to give her
two days off a week, Wednesdays and Saturdays.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:58.290
Girl... you're letting that towel
cool down way too much.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.660
Today you'd like the back
and neck course, is that right?

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:03.960
Lukewarm.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.540
Good grief... I knew it.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:13.210
If Shirakawa-san was here, she'd set and fold
the towel when it was just hot enough not to hurt.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.920
Everything she does is so considerate,
it makes the perfect relaxing experience.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.460
Even just a little change can ruin it...

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.290
And this girl is terrible.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.460
At the very least, I'll use this time to meditate.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.670
Wow, your back is so stiff!

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.050
It's like a rock!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.670
With a back this stiff,
doesn't it cause you a lot of problems?

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.840
Well, that's exactly the reason why I come here...

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.340
Ah, that would make sense!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.750
My short trip is a failure...

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:47.210
Now I have to go back to work with things
even worse than they were before.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:53.380
Matsukata, you haven't finished
that collaborative project yet?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.790
Hurry up and get it done.
We need enough time to check it.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.800
Yessir...

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.920
Now then... back to work.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.960
It's no good.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.170
I can't get motivated at all.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:15.630
Journey to
Yakushima

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.290
A full spread collaborative article,
sponsored by a travel agency...

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.050
"Journey to Yakushima."

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.710
"A holiday for adults."

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:23.210
"Experience the island's mysteries."

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.790
"The perfect short trip for any weekend,
with access directly from the airport"...?!

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.080
Don't cheapen the value of a World Heritage Site!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.130
So tell me exactly, what aspect
of the project makes it feel cheap to you?

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.040
The frivolous marketing terms
they want you to use?

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.500
Or maybe the fact that it will be used to attract
tourists who will trample all over its natural beauty?

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:45.670
Both.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:50.300
It's already set to be published in this issue,
so I have no choice.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.210
But you know...

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.590
When it came to writing this article,
I didn't want to just accept it without a fight.

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.460
But all I could come up with were things
that are ultimately out of my hands.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.960
You're making such a big deal out of this...
It's just a sponsored travel article.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:09.460
Yakushima is a major tourist destination, but people
don't come unless somebody advertises. Right?

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.750
Sometimes in order to finish a job,
I just have to stop thinking entirely.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.840
When I do, it's surprising how easily
I can get things done...

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:23.880
...almost as if there was never even
a problem in the first place.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:28.630
Hello?

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.920
Matsukata-san? I'm sorry about last week.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:36.630
If you've got some time this evening,
there's still room for a reservation.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.540
Yay! Put me down!

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.080
Midoriko Shirakawa (29)
Massage Therapist

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:45.000
It's been 5 years since I quit my office job
and started this career.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:49.050
I enjoy providing relaxation to people
who suffer from stiffness.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.000
Neck muscles strained from stress...

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.500
Arms sore from overuse...

00:05:56.210 --> 00:06:00.920
I'm happy to be able to return people
to a normal state of being.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:02.460
However...

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.920
Days off?

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.830
One a week is the best I can do.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.250
You're the main masseuse here.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:13.510
But, in reality I've only been taking off
one day every two weeks.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.790
That's because you go out of your way to call
and make reservations for clients.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.170
And as a result,
you've even been getting paid more.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.290
The job that I enjoy
and have never gotten tired of...

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.550
Lately I find... it's been...

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:31.830
Th-that hurts...!

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:37.960
I'm sorry about that.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:38.750
Huh?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.620
About what?

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.920
I'm feeling refreshed after that!

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.840
Oh, really? Then that's a relief-

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:52.710
It's because you spend too much energy
on each individual customer.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:56.080
I might not have been able to relieve
all your stiffness today.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:00.000
Matsukata-san, you're always
the most tense customer that I have.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.710
Because I do a job that induces it...

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.040
Ah, it's gotten late.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.710
I went 10 minutes over again...

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:14.510
She always has such a calm demeanor
that I end up taking my time without realizing it.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:17.920
But... somehow she seems different today...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.460
I'll be waiting for you outside.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.460
Ah, okay.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.000
Maybe I'm just imagining it.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.710
You have to focus harder on being more efficient.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.000
Right...

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.710
You've kept the next customer waiting, you know.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.000
I'm sorry.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:40.290
The extended time...
Shirakawa-san got in trouble for it.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.920
Thank you for coming today.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.170
We always appreciate your business.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:56.510
Doing an earnest job and being sincere in your
work is not always what people want from you...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.000
...or so it seems.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.870
But that's not...

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.210
I'm exhausted.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.870
Okay, that's all. Thank you for your patience.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.010
Oh, that pose...

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.080
Matsukata-san made it earlier, too...

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.710
How do you feel?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.160
I wonder if it's just because I fell asleep,
but... I feel sluggish.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.880
She doesn't feel refreshed...

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:29.300
I'm not satisfied.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:32.410
I thought I had made up my mind
when I sat down to write this.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.410
But seeing it printed in the magazine like this...

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.800
I question the reason
I even did it in the first place...

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.090
Senpai!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.790
The response to this issue
has been really amazing, apparently!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.710
In Yakushima!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.670
The travel agency said the amount of people
calling their office is at least 2, if not 3, times more!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:48.670
They just called to extend their gratitude to-

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.080
What's wrong?

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:55.290
Why would you throw your own article on the floor?

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.120
Senpa- Ah! She ran away!

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.000
Do you remember the article I wrote two years ago,

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:09.830
"The Decaying World Heritage Site:
Yakushima's Future"?

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:13.290
I don't recall.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.210
Back then... although I knew it was
the primary industry for local business,

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:21.710
I still made complaints against the tourism board
and travel agencies for their lack of accountability.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.750
Now all of a sudden, I find myself
writing an article that says,

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:32.330
"Yakushima is a great place,
hurry and come on down."

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.800
You take everything too seriously.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.120
There's nothing you can change by lingering on it.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:45.370
On top of that, I can't find the right answer.
No matter how much thought I put into it.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.880
Obviously. Because there is no right answer.

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.370
I wonder if that's true...

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.710
You know...

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:59.620
If you put energy into reflecting on every single
article you've ever written, then... you'll burn out!

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:06.290
Ah, Hiro?

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.790
Sorry, they sprung a work dinner
on us last minute. So, today...

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.670
Okay, I understand.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.630
I'll cancel our reservation.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.170
I'm really sorry!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:24.840
Oh, look who's back!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.540
I see you've made yourself quite stiff again.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.920
Matsukata-san...?

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:40.590
Somehow...

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:47.500
I didn't find an answer to my problem,
despite striving to find one.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:52.000
Now I only have regret...
about what I created as a result.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:53.630
That's why I'm so stiff.

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.210
Ow! Ow, ow!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.040
Ow! Ow, ow!
This acupuncture point is linked to your head.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.210
It hurts quite a bit, yes?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.460
Beyond pain... I'd say anguish!

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:04.290
So, you feel regret?

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.210
Huh?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.460
About the end result you created?

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:11.580
No...

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.580
About the fact you didn't find an answer?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:15.630
No...

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.710
Then what exactly are you regretful about?

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:20.170
Um...

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.040
It's not a regret like, "I wish
I would've gone in that direction instead"...

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:29.340
It's just that, I think I'm regretting the fact
that I gave up in the end.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.250
I can't shake the idea that there was something
more I could have done before I gave up.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:40.040
Regardless of how things turned out, if I had just
done that, I think I would be satisfied with myself.

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:46.790
At least, that's how I'm explaining it to myself.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.210
Oh, I forgot.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:01.460
I'm sorry I stayed too long last time.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:02.460
Huh?

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.170
I kept track of the time today.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:07.130
It's fine, don't worry about it.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:09.510
Please take your time to change.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.750
I can't keep going like this.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:18.290
I don't like working at a place
that makes tired people fuss and worry.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.710
And I don't want to cut their time short
just to maximize efficiency.

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:26.040
What exactly it is... that I want?

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.120
I want to raise the spirits of my customers.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:32.460
I want them to return home
with a soothed body and clear mind.

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.920
Giving that up... will only lead to regrets later!

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.760
Owner... I need to speak with you.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:43.250
What?

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:46.910
I'm thinking about quitting this job.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.080
Wait, are you serious?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.790
I'm sorry this is so sudden.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.870
If you quit now, what do you think
will happen to this store?

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.630
What are you unsatisfied with?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.130
It's difficult right now,
but if this is about your salary, then-

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.510
It's not a problem with my salary.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.500
Then are you telling me
you want to go independent?

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:04.830
That's not it, either.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.210
By shortening the courses
to fit more customers into our schedules,

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:11.380
everyone also lost the time necessary
to regain their composure.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.500
Everything here now feels rushed and stressful...

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:19.330
I don't believe I can truly refresh my customers
in a place like this!

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:25.790
Huh?

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.170
What was this, again?

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.420
Damn it, I'm forgetting all sorts of things.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:38.500
Dear Matsukata-sama,
I wonder if you still remember me.
I'm Oki from the Youth Association.
We met when you came to Yakushima to research a story.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.550
Dear Matsukata-sama,

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.500
I wonder if you still remember me.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.500
Only for this moment

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.760
I'm Oki from the Youth Association.

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.250
We met 2 years ago when you came
to Yakushima to research a story.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:49.920
We laugh together softly

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.050
I read your new article the other day.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:49.800
Thank you for introducing
our island to your audience.

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:53.040
Thanks to you, the Tourism Association
is in high spirits.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:55.250
And that's just fine

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.420
I-I looked so young...

00:13:55.580 --> 00:14:00.000
I was able to print some pictures from back then.
I'm sending them along with a few recent ones.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:04.790
We bathe in a bead of light that envelops us

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.340
Matsukata!

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:08.250
As we fall asleep

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.540
The meeting is about to start.

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:08.330
Coming.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.630
Once again someone is singing tonight

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.210
I thought about it so hard,
and still couldn't come up with an answer.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:21.840
But while I was struggling, I never realized... nature
was flourishing stronger than I could ever imagine.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:20.830
Conveying the past into the night sky

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:27.590
And the tomorrow I'll spend

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.750
I was touched by that letter,
and by nature's resilience.

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.790
Deep down, it should've made me happy.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:33.710
Joking with you

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.460
I really wanted it to... but something's missing.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:34.590
Matsukata.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:39.790
Baby, the gentle night has come

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:37.210
I noticed you didn't have any pitches
ready for the meeting, but...

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.000
I won't accept excuses like,
"I couldn't think of anything good

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:45.670
Baby, now all that's left is tomorrow

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.960
because something was on my mind."

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.880
I want to see 10 of them next week.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:53.340
Baby, this wasn't how it was supposed to be, right?

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:50.420
If you stop even just briefly,
it takes time to get moving again!

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:52.090
Right.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.500
I'm at a standstill right now.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.410
Oh, yes it is

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.710
Did something get stuck
and bring all my gears to a halt?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.330
Baby baby

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.460
No... perhaps I'm just not working
to get those gears moving.

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:07.330
Maybe I'll go get another massage...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:12.500
Better not. For some reason, they don't leave me
as relaxed as they used to.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:13.790
Matsukata-san?

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:16.000
Shirakawa-san!

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.750
What? You're going to quit?

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.960
I got lucky, a person
at a health center reached out to me

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:25.630
looking for someone to run their massage clinic.

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:27.420
I agreed to it right away.

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.710
Wow, that's really fortunate!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:37.630
I was surprised because this all happened the day
after I told the owner that I was going to quit.

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:41.630
I've been struggling because I felt that continuing to
work there wasn't aligning with my personal goals.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.420
And that was starting to affect my hands.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.460
Hands?

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:46.840
Yes. Our hands reflect ourselves.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:51.000
The way we live our lives...
and the emotions we feel at any particular moment.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:55.710
This all started because of what you said
the last time I saw you, Matsukata-san.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:57.710
What exactly did I say?

00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.590
You said you regretted giving up.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.130
After hearing that, I made up my mind.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.960
I was unsure about what to do for a long time.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.130
So, thank you very much.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:12.210
Ah, no, not at all. I didn't do anything...

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:14.120
Goodbye then.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.010
See you again.

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.120
She... actually thanked me.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:25.040
Shirakawa-san was able to properly think it over
before she gave up and found her answer.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.500
What am I doing?

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.920
Giving up and dragging along...

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.130
all of my regrets.

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:36.920
One more time.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.420
I'll think it over... without giving up.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.080
Have you already left your previous position?

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:47.290
Not yet.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.960
Right now, my final shift is at the end of this week.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:52.500
Okay, then you can start
from next month as we discussed.

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.250
Sure.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:57.000
Um... is it always this busy on weekdays?

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:58.880
Yes, I'd say so.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:01.210
The weekends are even more busy.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:07.130
Most people tend to want the 30
or 45 minute course, so it's always very packed.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.090
But... with so many people,
it would be impossible for me to handle alone.

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:12.910
Then how about we make plans to hire
one more person to join you?

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:17.000
If we consider putting you on a rotation,
then having two beds would be best.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:20.630
Well, even by yourself you could leave
the automated massage device

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:21.960
hooked into the other bed and...

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:34.170
Excuse me, I have to leave right at
the 30 minute mark, so hurry it up.

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.300
Ah, okay. I understand.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:40.710
But... this knot in her back
will come undone really soon.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.210
Just one more minute...

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:48.090
Hey... I'm seriously in a hurry here.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.210
Right!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.750
Jeez, I'm already beyond late.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.210
What I said to the owner before was arrogant.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:59.340
"People can't feel refreshed
in a store that rushes them."

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:03.410
Will I really be able to accomplish
anything different at my next job?

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:09.050
A soothed body and clear mind...
can I actually offer that to everyone?

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:12.590
Shirakawa-san, the next customer is waiting for you.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.500
Coming.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.460
These are...

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.880
Don't go rummaging around
on other people's desks.

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:27.260
Did you go... to Yakushima?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.580
Yeah.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.170
The sky there is... always so blue.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:35.460
Huh?

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.960
Regardless of what happens beneath it...

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:43.370
Whether people trample on or destroy
the environment there... the sky doesn't change.

00:18:44.630 --> 00:18:46.340
Always vast and blue...

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.760
Our hands reflect ourselves.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:59.080
The way we live our lives... and the emotions
we feel at any particular moment.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.250
I'm finished. 10 new pitches.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.800
Just leave them there.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.630
Well, most of them aren't too bad, but...

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:34.170
What's up with this?

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:37.120
"Don't Cheapen the Value
of a World Heritage Site"...?

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:41.170
Unless I submit that... I can't move forward.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.500
Well it gets filed... here.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:04.630
I want to believe that I made the right decision.

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:07.500
I want a job that I can do without any regrets.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:12.920
Even if that's only an ideal... or just a silly fantasy...

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.500
Thanks for your patience.

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:25.090
Right on time.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:29.130
My body... feels light.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.750
I feel so refreshed!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.210
Matsukata-san... your chest is showing.

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:44.960
Thank you very much for
your patronage all this time.

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:48.540
My pleasure. Please do your best at your next job.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:49.710
Of course.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.500
I'll definitely come visit you there sometime.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.330
I'll be waiting there for you.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:21:05.000
Midoriko Shirakawa (29)
Massage Therapist

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.080
"That felt wonderful."

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:02.090
The happiest moment for me
is hearing those words from a customer...

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:05.010
Frankly, it's the saving grace of this job.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.830
Creating that moment is the most important thing...
and it must be strived for.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.630
I only realized that after
I decided to leave this shop.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.000
Now all that's left for me is to move onward.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.510
Shangri-la

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:37.750
Yume no naka de sae umaku waraenai kimi no koto

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:43.080
Dame na hitotte shikari nagara aishiteitai

00:21:46.290 --> 00:21:50.040
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:53.620
Bokura doko he mukaouka

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:59.090
Ahh... ahh...

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.340
Shangri-la

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:06.290
Shiawasedatte sakende kureyo

00:22:06.290 --> 00:22:10.580
Ijippari na kimi no nakigao misete kureyo

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.250
Shangri-la

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:17.250
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai boku no koto

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:22.290
Dame na hitotte shikarinagara ashitekure

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:25.500
Shinji
Nice Work Today
Do your best, but don't
wear yourself out.
-Shinji

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.830
Next Episode: Reward Man
